# Phosphor theme

Full doctrine: `docs/design/PHOSPHOR-THEME.md`  
**Issues / thinking / fixes (look here first):** `docs/design/PHOSPHOR-LESSONS-AND-RUNBOOK.md`

## Non-negotiables

- **No purple.** Brand is green → teal → soft gold (`--brand-violet` is a legacy name).
- Edit visuals in **`:root` / `.dark` tokens** or shared utilities — do not paste new brand hex in components.
- Dark mode: `@theme inline` must use `var(...)`. Never bake surface colors as literal RGB in `@theme`.
- Prefer `bg-bg` / `bg-paper` / `bg-elevated` / `text-ink` over `bg-white` / `text-black`.

## Reuse these

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Brand fill | `.bg-brand-gradient` |
| Feature icon | `landingIconTileClass` |
| Break (special) | `landingIconCrystalClass` + `glassSurfaceClass` |
| Section type (marketing) | `landingEyebrowClass` + `landingH2Class` + `landingLeadClass` |
| Type scale (hub / lessons) | `docs/design/PHOSPHOR-THEME.md` §2 — Bricolage / Hanken / Space Mono + size ladder |
| Logo mark | `brandMarkClass` / `brandMarkSmClass` |
| Final CTA | `ctaPanelClass` |
| Page width | `max-w-[var(--layout-max)]` or `SectionBand` |
| Hub main stage | `HUB_MAIN_CLASS` (`bg-paper` vs sidebar `bg-bg`) |

## Break signature

Same gradient as sibling steps. Crystal glaze **only** on Break. Do not reintroduce a solid yellow Break icon.

## Before shipping UI

Light + dark both look correct; `min-w-0` on flex children; no one-off glass/glow stacks when a utility already exists.
